  "name": "Question 13",
  "problem": "Which of the following systems are homogeneous?\n\n- ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 3\\end{aligned}]x(t)$\n- ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 1\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$\n- ${x}^{\u2032}(t)=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}]x(t)+[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)\\end{aligned}]$",
  "worked_solution": "In matrix form, the system\n\n$$\n{x}^{\u2032}(t)=A(t)x(t)+f(t)\n$$\n\nis *homogeneous* when $f\u22610,$ and *inhomogeneous* when $f\u22620.$\n\nWith this in mind, let's inspect each system:\n\n- System I is homogeneous since $f\u22610.$\n\n- System II is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}t \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]\u22620.$\n\n- System III is inhomogeneous since $f=[\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(t) \\\\ \\operatorname{sin}\u2061(t)\\end{aligned}]\u22620.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only\".",
